@page "/guest"
@inject RemoteSupport.Platform.Services.PayloadService Payloads
@{
    // Outside help, step 3 (3.9, 2026-10-06): the guest console's page. For somebody with NO account
    // here — a customer's accounting firm — whom the customer has given a code. Public, and the same
    // for everybody: the console it offers belongs to no company and asks for nothing but the code.
    ViewData["Title"] = "Connect with a code";
}
<section class="section">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:760px">
        <h1>Connect to a computer with a code</h1>
        <p class="muted" style="font-size:18px">
            Somebody has given you a nine-digit code so that you can help them on their computer. Use it here in
            your browser, or with the guest console. You do not need an account.
        </p>
        <div class="card" style="margin-top:20px">
            <h3 style="margin-top:0">How it works</h3>
            <ol style="line-height:1.7">
                <li>Choose <strong>Connect in this browser</strong>, or download the guest console. Nothing is installed either way.</li>
                <li>Type your name, your company if you have one, and the code. A code lasts ten minutes and works once.</li>
                <li>Whoever gave you the code is shown your name and lets you in — the person at the computer, or their IT company's technician, who is in the session with you. Their IT company is told, and can watch and end it.</li>
                <li>You can see their screen and use the mouse and keyboard — files only if they allow it, and no tools. Leave, or close the window, when you are done.</li>
            </ol>
            @* Both ways in (Clint, answer 3): this browser, with nothing to download, or the program. *@
            <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap">
                <a class="btn btn-accent" href="/guest/web">Connect in this browser</a>
                @if (Payloads.TechnicianExeAvailable) { <a class="btn" href="/guest/console.exe">Download the guest console</a> }
            </div>
            <p class="muted" style="font-size:13px;margin-top:10px">
                The browser needs nothing installed. The guest console is for Windows@(Payloads.TechnicianExeAvailable ? "; if Windows asks whether to run it, choose Run" : " and is not available on this server yet").
            </p>
        </div>
        <p class="muted" style="font-size:13px;margin-top:16px">
            Nobody legitimate will ever phone you and ask you to read out a code from your own screen. A code is for
            the person who asked you for help to give to you, never the other way round.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>
